 "text": "Hi, how are you today? For a typical commuting or trail bike, air in the tires holds up pretty well. I'd usually check them once a month and pump them up if they've dropped a few psi. A good rule of thumb is never let the pressure drop below what's written on the sidewall. Lower numbers are fine, just don't go below the max. Guessing is generally a bad plan. A digital gauge is under ten bucks and gives you a much more accurate reading. Go a little lower, but never so low that the sidewalls are at risk. Lower pressures are nice on smooth roads, but they increase the risk of pinch flats.",
